    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "`MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))` focuses on the file but the anchor is the immediate parent of the file. i'd like it to be rooted at the cwd the same way as `MiniFiles.open()` , just opening however many levels deep of nested directory as needed.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))</code> focuses on the file but the anchor is the immediate parent of the file. i'd like it to be rooted at the cwd the same way as <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.open()</code> , just opening however many levels deep of nested directory as needed.</p>",
    "bodyText": "MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0)) focuses on the file but the anchor is the immediate parent of the file. i'd like it to be rooted at the cwd the same way as MiniFiles.open() , just opening however many levels deep of nested directory as needed.",
