                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "wouldn't it be possible to add a flag to the third argument to `MiniFiles.open` that when set you call `reveal_cwd` when the explorer opens? I tried to recreate it using the `MiniFilesBufferCreate` event but I couldn't figure out a neat way to get the opts, except a separate global variable. \r\n\r\nAdding this code works\r\n```lua\r\nMiniFiles.open = function(path, use_latest, opts)\r\n   -- Existing Code\r\n   -- ....\r\n\r\n\tif explorer.opts.options.reveal_cwd_on_open then\r\n\t\tMiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\r\n\tend\r\nend\r\n\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">wouldn't it be possible to add a flag to the third argument to <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFiles.open</code> that when set you call <code class=\"notranslate\">reveal_cwd</code> when the explorer opens? I tried to recreate it using the <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesBufferCreate</code> event but I couldn't figure out a neat way to get the opts, except a separate global variable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adding this code works</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"MiniFiles.open = function(path, use_latest, opts)\n   -- Existing Code\n   -- ....\n\n\tif explorer.opts.options.reveal_cwd_on_open then\n\t\tMiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\n\tend\nend\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniFiles</span>.<span class=\"pl-en\">open</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">path</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">use_latest</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">opts</span>)\n   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> Existing Code</span>\n   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> ....</span>\n\n\t<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">explorer</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">opts</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">options</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">reveal_cwd_on_open</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n\t\t<span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniFiles</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">reveal_cwd</span>()\n\t<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "wouldn't it be possible to add a flag to the third argument to MiniFiles.open that when set you call reveal_cwd when the explorer opens? I tried to recreate it using the MiniFilesBufferCreate event but I couldn't figure out a neat way to get the opts, except a separate global variable.\nAdding this code works\nMiniFiles.open = function(path, use_latest, opts)\n   -- Existing Code\n   -- ....\n\n\tif explorer.opts.options.reveal_cwd_on_open then\n\t\tMiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\n\tend\nend",
