                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "Yes, `MiniFilesExplorerOpen` was added as a reaction to #817, as a way for external tools/plugins to act on user opening explorer.\r\n\r\nFor this particular case of \"automatically reveal cwd for explorer opened at file\", I'd suggest writing own wrapper. So something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal open_at_buf_file = function()\r\n  MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))\r\n  MiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\r\nend\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>ef', open_at_buf_file)\r\n```",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniFilesExplorerOpen</code> was added as a reaction to <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2247328784\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/817\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/817/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/817\">#817</a>, as a way for external tools/plugins to act on user opening explorer.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For this particular case of \"automatically reveal cwd for explorer opened at file\", I'd suggest writing own wrapper. So something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local open_at_buf_file = function()\n  MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))\n  MiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\nend\nvim.keymap.set('n', '&lt;Leader&gt;ef', open_at_buf_file)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">open_at_buf_file</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniFiles</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">open</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_get_name</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>))\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">MiniFiles</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">reveal_cwd</span>()\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>&lt;Leader&gt;ef<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">open_at_buf_file</span>)</pre></div>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, MiniFilesExplorerOpen was added as a reaction to #817, as a way for external tools/plugins to act on user opening explorer.\nFor this particular case of \"automatically reveal cwd for explorer opened at file\", I'd suggest writing own wrapper. So something like this:\nlocal open_at_buf_file = function()\n  MiniFiles.open(vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(0))\n  MiniFiles.reveal_cwd()\nend\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>ef', open_at_buf_file)",
